# Copy to back-end/.dockerignore AND back-end/.gcloudignore (same content).
# Cloud Build uploads what .gcloudignore lets through (the tarball stays in the
# project's <project>_cloudbuild bucket), then docker build filters by
# .dockerignore. The secret patterns mean the same in both syntaxes (`**/` = any
# depth, a leading `/` = this folder only); plain names like `.git` match only at
# the top in .dockerignore but at any depth in .gcloudignore, which is harmless.

# --- Secrets: never in a build context (SKILL.md rule 8) ----------------------
# A `RUN rm` after `COPY . /app/` does NOT take a file out of the image: it stays
# in the COPY layer, readable by anyone who can pull the image.
**/.env*
**/.config
/vars

# --- Not part of the image ----------------------------------------------------
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
.git
/tests
